,"gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"is like this indeed"},{"surface":"தெற்றென","parts":[{"text":"தெற்றென","lemma":"தெற்றென","gloss":"clearly"}],"gloss":"clearly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யாரா","parts":[{"text":"யாரா","lemma":"யாரா","gloss":"who"}],"gloss":"who","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குவர்கொல்","parts":[{"text":"குவர்கொல்","lemma":"குவர்கொல்","gloss":"will they become"}],"gloss":"will they become","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தாமே","parts":[{"text":"தாம்","lemma":"தாம்","gloss":"themselves"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"themselves indeed"},{"surface":"நேரிழை","parts":[{"text":"நேர்","lemma":"நேர்","gloss":"fine"},{"text":"இழை","lemma":"இழை","gloss":"jewels"}],"gloss":"fine jewels"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உருத்த","parts":[{"text":"உருத்த","lemma":"உரு","gloss":"prominent"}],"gloss":"prominent"},{"surface":"பல்சுணங்கு","parts":[{"text":"பல்","lemma":"பல்","gloss":"many"},{"text":"சுணங்கு","lemma":"சுணங்கு","gloss":"beauty spots"}],"gloss":"many beauty spots"},{"surface":"அணிந்த","parts":[{"text":"அணிந்த","lemma":"அணி","gloss":"adorned"}],"gloss":"adorned"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மருப்புஇள","parts":[{"text":"மருப்பு","lemma":"மருப்பு","gloss":"tusk-like"},{"text":"இள","lemma":"இள","gloss":"young"}],"gloss":"tusk-like young"},{"surface":"வனமுலை","parts":[{"text":"வன","lemma":"வன","gloss":"beautiful"},{"text":"முலை","lemma":"முலை","gloss":"breasts"}],"gloss":"beautiful breasts"},{"surface":"ஞெமுக்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஞெமுக்கு","lemma":"ஞெமுக்கு","gloss":"to press"}],"gloss":"to press"},{"surface":"வோரே","parts":[{"text":"வோர்","lemma":"வோர்","gloss":"those who do"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"those who do indeed"}]}],"literal":"The lord of the Chola country, with his roaring ocean-like army, / even if they are wealthy rulers of the earth under a sheltering umbrella, / those who went singing, leaving behind their sword-strength, / every time they come, their hearts blossom ... / with unceasing giving, having large hands adorned with shining bangles, / like the cool mountain pool of Pari's Parambu hill, / she has become rare to behold, and with excellent / womanhood filled with splendor, adorned, / swaying like spread fine cloth, coolly, / where the fragrant smoke of eaglewood gently went and settled, / with the fragrance smelling in the reddish tall mansion, / she is now confined to the house, she of the bright forehead. / Since it is not like that, clearly guarding, / feeding balls of ripe paddy rice, in every grove, / they guard with fierce-eyed elephants; and besides, / the kings do not cease to come. Her brothers, / who have conquered in fighting battles, holding long, terrifying spears, / have terrifying heads smeared with blood. / And their valor is also like this. Clearly, / who will they be, indeed, / adorned with prominent, many beauty spots, / who will press her young, beautiful, tusk-like breasts?","translation":"The lord of the Chola country, with his roaring ocean-like army, and other wealthy rulers of the earth under sheltering umbrellas, might come. But those bards who went singing, leaving their swords behind, find their hearts blossoming every time they arrive... Like the cool mountain pool of Pari's Parambu hill, famed for unceasing giving from hands adorned with shining bangles, she has become rare to behold. Filled with the splendor of excellent womanhood, adorned, swaying like fine cloth, she is now confined to her house, she of the bright forehead, where the fragrant smoke of eaglewood gently settles, filling the reddish tall mansion with aroma. Since she is not easily won, they guard her vigilantly, feeding balls of ripe paddy to fierce-eyed elephants in every grove. Yet, the kings do not cease to come. Her brothers, who have conquered in fierce battles, hold long, terrifying spears and have heads smeared with blood. Their valor is of such a fierce nature. Who indeed will they be, who will embrace her young, beautiful, tusk-like breasts, adorned with many beauty spots, she who wears fine jewels?","modern":"ஒலிக்கும் கடல் போன்ற படையைக் கொண்ட சோழ நாட்டுத் தலைவனும், குடை நிழலில் உலகை ஆளும் பிற செல்வந்தர்களான அரசர்களும் அவளைப் பெற விரும்பினாலும், வாள் வலிமையைக் கைவிட்டுப் பாடிச் சென்ற பாணர்கள் அவளது வள்ளல் தன்மையைக் கண்டு நெஞ்சம் மலர்கின்றனர். விளங்கும் வளையல்களை அணிந்த, கொடைத்தன்மை மிக்க பாரியின் பறம்பு மலையிலுள்ள குளிர்ந்த சுனை நீரைப் போல, காண்பதற்கு அரியவளாகி, சிறந்த பெண்மை நலம் நிறைந்து, மெல்லிய ஆடை அசைவது போல அசைந்து, அகில் புகையின் நறுமணம் கமழும் பெரிய மாளிகையில் அந்த ஒளி பொருந்திய நெற்றியை உடையவள் இப்போது வீட்டிற்குள் செறித்து வைக்கப்பட்டுள்ளாள். நிலைமை இவ்வாறு இருப்பதால், அவளைக் காவல் காக்க, சோலைகள் தோறும் நெற்கவளங்களை ஊட்டிச் சினங்கொண்ட யானைகளை நிறுத்தியுள்ளனர். ஆயினும் அரசர்கள் அவளை வேண்டி வருவதை நிறுத்தவில்லை. அவளுடைய சகோதரர்களோ போர்க்களங்களை வென்றவர்கள்; குருதி படிந்த அச்சம் தரும் நீண்ட வேல்களையும், பகைவரின் வெட்டப்பட்ட தலைகளையும் உடையவர்கள். இத்தகைய வீரத்தைக் கொண்ட இவர்களது காவலையும் மீறி, அழகிய அணிகலன்களையும் தேமல் படர்ந்த இளமையான அழகிய மார்பகங்களையும் உடைய இவளைத் தழுவப் போகும் வீரன் யாரோ?","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Puram genre, specifically the Makaṭpāṟ Kāñci theme, where kings demand a girl in marriage, but her fierce brothers refuse, leading to impending war. An onlooker or poet describes the beauty of a young woman of a warrior clan, comparing her to the rare, cool mountain pool of Pari's Parambu hill. She is kept confined inside her house, which is filled with the fragrant smoke of eaglewood. Outside, her brothers guard her vigilantly, feeding fierce-eyed war elephants with balls of ripe paddy in every grove. Her brothers are terrifying warriors who have slain enemies in battle and hold blood-smeared spears. Despite this danger, kings do not cease to come to claim her, and the poet wonders who the brave man will be who can overcome these fierce brothers and win her hand.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.1],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,1.8],[1.8,2.3],[2.3,2.6],[2